=== B. FINRA 5250: payments for market making ===
5250 is a different prohibition from already-taught PFOF / Rule 606
5250(a): no member or person associated with a member shall accept any payment or other consideration,
  directly or indirectly, from an issuer of a security, or any affiliate or promoter thereof,
  for publishing a quotation, acting as market maker in a security, or submitting an application in connection therewith
  issuer / affiliate / promoter payment for acting as market maker: prohibited? True
  already-taught PFOF for routing customer orders is the same prohibition? False
5250(b) official exceptions exist: payment for bona fide services, including investment banking services
  (including underwriting compensation and fees); reimbursement of SEC or state registration fees and SRO listing fees;
  and any payment expressly provided for under the rules of a national securities exchange
  that are effective after being filed with, or filed with and approved by, the SEC
  this toy builds a promoter / 5121-affiliate / exchange-fee-schedule engine? False
  every issuer-paid service is banned? False
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
assertions passed: 8/8
=== C. FINRA 5270: front running of block transactions ===
5270 is a different prohibition from already-taught FINRA 5320
5270(a): a member with material, non-public market information concerning an imminent block transaction
  may not cause an order in that security or a related financial instrument to be executed
  prior to the time information concerning the block transaction has been made publicly available
  or has otherwise become stale or obsolete
  this is the already-taught 5320 trading-ahead-of-a-held-customer-equity-order rule? False
SM .03: in equity securities, a transaction involving 10,000 shares or more is generally deemed to be a block transaction,
  although a transaction of fewer than 10,000 shares could be considered a block transaction
  10,000 shares is a rigid floor? False
A block transaction that has been agreed upon does not lose its identity as such by arranging for
  partial executions of the full transaction in portions which themselves are not of block size
  if the execution of the full transaction may have a material impact on the market
SM .02: public availability will not be satisfied until the entire block transaction has been completed and publicly reported
  a print of part of the block makes the entire block publicly available? False
official SM .04 exceptions exist; this toy is not an information-barrier / consent / exchange-leg engine
  this toy builds an information-barrier / consent / exchange-leg engine? False
SM .05: front running of non-block orders may still violate other FINRA rules, including Rule 2010 and already-taught Rule 5320
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
assertions passed: 12/12
=== D. FINRA 5230: payments involving publications that influence the market price ===
5230 is a different prohibition from already-taught FINRA 5250
5230(a): except as provided in paragraph (b), no member shall, directly or indirectly,
  give, permit to be given, or offer to give, anything of value to any person
  for the purpose of influencing or rewarding the action of such person
  in connection with the publication or circulation in any electronic or other public media,
  including any investment service or similar publication, Web site, newspaper,
  magazine or other periodical, radio, or television program,
  of any matter that has, or is intended to have, an effect upon the market price of any security
  this is the already-taught 5250 issuer-payment-for-market-making rule? False
5230(b) official exceptions exist: (1) a communication clearly distinguishable as paid advertising;
  (2) a communication that discloses the receipt of compensation and the amount thereof
  in accordance with Section 17(b) of the Securities Act;
  (3) a research report as defined in Rule 2241
  this toy builds a Section 17(b) or Rule 2241 engine? False
  every paid communication is banned? False
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
assertions passed: 15/15
=== E. FINRA 5280: trading ahead of research reports ===
5280 is a different prohibition from already-taught FINRA 5270 and 5320
5280(a): No member shall establish, increase, decrease or liquidate an inventory position
  in a security or a derivative of such security based on non-public advance knowledge
  of the content or timing of a research report in that security
  this is the already-taught 5270 front-running-of-an-imminent-block rule? False
  this is the already-taught 5320 trading-ahead-of-a-held-customer-equity-order rule? False
5280(b): a member must establish, maintain and enforce policies and procedures reasonably designed
  to restrict or limit the information flow between research department personnel,
  or other persons with knowledge of the content or timing of a research report,
  and trading department personnel, so as to prevent trading department personnel
  from utilizing non-public advance knowledge of the issuance or content of a research report
  for the benefit of the member or any other person
official 5280(b) information-flow procedures exist; this toy is not that engine
  this toy builds an information-barrier or Rule 2241 research-report definition engine? False
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
